result.notes:
Method. I went through all 38 page files (about 30k lines), one at a time, for every digit mechanism:
- the shared formatNumber, formatDate, formatDateTime and formatBusinessDateTime;
- Intl and toLocale* calls in any locale, including calls with no argument;
- 'ar-EG' and bare 'ar';
- ai, aiAmount, toArabicDigits and readerDigits;
- hard-coded U+0660-0669;
- {{x}} params passed to t().

I then followed every component and lib a page imports, using an import-graph script, to the place where the digits are decided. I checked each shared/ui and shared/lib module a Fleet page uses: NumberedPager/FleetPager, MultiSelect, DataTable groups, FileUpload, StatCard, print-window and xlsx-writer are Latin or not reached. I parsed the Arabic catalogue (13,897 keys) for Arabic-Indic digits, and read the 36 page specs plus the Fleet module specs that render these pages.

Findings:
1. In the page files themselves, the ONLY Arabic-Indic mechanisms are 40 calls of the shared formatNumber (13) and formatDate (27), on 39 lines in 17 pages, plus two Arabic catalogue values: OdometerPage «اعرض آخر ١٢ شهر» and the FleetSettingsPage hint «(من ١ إلى ٣٠)».
2. No page uses formatDateTime, formatBusinessDateTime, a bare 'ar' or 'ar-EG' Intl, or toLocale* with the UI locale. Every page-local Intl is en-US or ar-EG-u-nu-latn.
3. Every on-screen board TABLE is already Latin (ymd, LATIN, FigureChip, FleetPager). The Arabic-Indic figures an Arabic reader still sees are:
   - (a) the toolbar counts on «التمامات», «السيارات», «التوكيل», «خصم الإيصالات», «السائقون», «عدادات السيارات», «مصروفات العهدة», «الإخطارات», «صيانة السيارات», «إنذارات الصيانة» and «التراخيص»;
   - (b) every date cell on the Fleet print sheets (FuelCards, Vehicles, Drivers, Dealership, Receipts, FuelCharging, Custody, LicenseExpenses, VehicleContracts), on the car and driver file prints (VehiclesList, VehicleDetail «طباعة التقرير», DriverProfile «طباعة الملف», DriverLicenseImage «طباعة الرخصة»), and on the receipt and dealership image prints;
   - (c) the Excel text-date columns;
   - (d) the dialogs and panels the pages host: the odometer and maintenance dialogs' km hints and dates, the accident transfer log, the dealership invoice dialog, the violations panels' counts and one MONEY total (CompanyViolationsPanel:698), the makes table «فترة الصيانة (كم)», and the image zoom readout;
   - (e) the custody Word letters «صرف/استعاضه/تسويه عهدة», which apply Arabic-Indic on purpose through ai/aiAmount/tatweelDate (the owner now wants these Latin too), and their on-screen copies in the charge dialog «نص الخطاب», the ledger drawer and the papers-setup preview.
4. The custody MEMO papers (custody-paper-memos), the licence-expense memo, the notice papers, the dashboard, the rosters and the fuel reconcile/repair screens are already Latin.

Recommended shape. Add one new Fleet-local file, apps/web/src/modules/fleet/lib/latin-figures.ts, lifted from VehicleDetailPage.tsx:143-163:
- latinNumber(v: number|null|undefined): en-US, or '—';
- latinDate(v: string|Date|null|undefined, locale): ar-EG-u-nu-latn / en-GB dateStyle medium, or '—';
- optionally latinDateTime.

Point every Fleet formatNumber and formatDate call at it; where a page already has a local LATIN (Odometer, Maintenance, MaintenanceAlarms), use that. In custody-paper-format.ts, drop ai, aiAmount and the AR_* constants, use grouped() for amounts, take ai out of tatweelDate, and fold the typed reason with asciiDigits. Give ZoomableImage an opt-in formatter prop, because Operations renders it. Edit four Arabic catalogue values (fleet.odometer.emptyMonth.action, fleet.settings.keys.odometerMissingReadingDaysHint, fleet.settings.intervalHint, fleet.vehicles.licenseImage.hint), plus fleet.odometer.sameAsPrevious, and optionally the dead fleet.dashboard.*VehiclesTitle and fleet.goLive.* keys. English stays byte-identical everywhere except the Arabic-only letters.

Size: about 12 page files, 12 component/lib files, the catalogue, and about 16 specs to re-point. The custody-paper-letters and custody-paper-format specs need the largest rewrite.

Identifiers (codes, plates, phones, national ids, the custody memo no), typed input values and numeric Excel cells were left alone, as instructed. Pages swept: 38. Spec files read for pins: 36 page specs, about 20 Fleet module and lib specs, and the component and lib files traced from the pages.
